<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanara</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Canara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kanara, or Canara, is the coastal region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>. Its ports, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mangalore">Mangalore</a>, Bhatkal and Honnavar, traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and other goods with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> and later the Portuguese. Under British rule it was divided into the districts of North Kanara and South Kanara.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanara.jpg" alt="Kanara" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raghu Naik NC · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
